1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:15,000
残酷な天使のように 少年よ 神話になれ

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:38,000
青い風が今 胸のドアを叩いても 私だけをただ見つめて 微笑んでるあなた

3
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
そっと触れるもの 求めることに夢中で

4
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
運命さえまだ知らない 痛いけな瞳

5
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
だけどいつか気づくでしょう その背中には

6
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:07,000
遥か未来 目指すための羽があること

7
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
残酷な天使の帝世 窓辺からやがて飛達

8
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:22,000
ほとばしる熱いパックスで 思い出を裏切るなら

9
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:30,000
この空を抱いて輝く 少年よ 神話になれ

10
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,000
神話になれ

11
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
神話になれ

12
00:01:44,000 --> 00:02:07,000
オープンに悩む

13
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,800
The unit one's awakened and been set free.

14
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,920
Zele sure won't stay quiet about this, will they?

15
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:15,200
This is insane.

16
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:19,080
The EVA series aren't capable of generating S2 organs themselves,

17
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:23,360
but we never imagined that one would be able to take one into itself this way.

18
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:27,160
This incident is at extreme odds with the scenario we created.

19
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:28,460
Gando Ikari.

20
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:32,540
It was a mistake to entrust nerve to him, wasn't it?

21
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:33,020
Hmm.

22
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:37,120
But he was the only one who could achieve this project's goals.

23
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:40,080
Ikari, what's going on in your mind?

24
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:41,460
It's begun at last.

25
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:44,300
Indeed, this is the beginning.

26
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,840
The damage the EVA incurred is beyond the Hendlick limit.

27
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:53,620
Yes.

28
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:56,820
It may be a while before we can restore everything to normal.

29
00:02:57,140 --> 00:03:00,300
Fortunately, the Magi system can be transferred to a new location.

30
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:02,620
We may be able to begin working as early as tomorrow.

31
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:05,640
This place isn't going to be viable anymore.

32
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:08,540
It's just a matter of time before they decide to abandon it.

33
00:03:08,720 --> 00:03:09,160
Mm-hmm.

34
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:10,120
Most likely.

35
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:13,500
But for the time being, we'll have to use the secondary control center.

36
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:15,160
Without the Magi?

37
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:15,960
Yes.

38
00:03:16,420 --> 00:03:19,220
We'll clean the dust off and be back in business by this afternoon.

39
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:23,160
But the chairs are too cramped down there, and the sensors don't operate smoothly.

40
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:25,160
It's difficult to work there.

41
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:28,660
Well, at least the layout is the same as our original control center.

42
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:31,000
At least we have an alternative.

43
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:35,120
We have no choice when it comes to using Unit 1.

44
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:43,920
It may be restrained by the cage, but are you sure it's safe?

45
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:50,960
Well, no heat emissions, free electrons, electromagnetic fields, or chemical reactions, and the S2 unit's completely inactive.

46
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:55,040
Nevertheless, on three separate occasions, Unit 1 has moved without power.

47
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:02,580
You can't judge this situation by just the things you can see.

48
00:04:02,860 --> 00:04:03,180
Uh-huh.

49
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:05,600
We sure can't take any chances, that's a fact.

50
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,720
It's as unpredictable as you are, Major.

51
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:11,140
Uh, sorry.

52
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:16,980
However, our concerns are not limited to Unit 1.

53
00:04:17,220 --> 00:04:17,700
Correct.

54
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:20,920
Serious damage was sustained by Unit 0 and 2.

55
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:24,620
Headquarters was partially destroyed, exposing Central Dogma.

56
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:28,120
We can't even estimate how much money and time have been lost.

57
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:31,360
This is because we didn't put a bell around Ikari's neck.

58
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:33,980
A bell was there, but it didn't ring.

59
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:36,640
A bell that doesn't ring has no purpose.

60
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:39,220
We'll make sure the bell works next time.

61
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:40,440
My, my.

62
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:42,660
What a completely unexpected situation.

63
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:45,480
How will you explain this to the committee?

64
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,060
I mean, to Sele?

65
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:48,740
There isn't anything to explain.

66
00:04:49,220 --> 00:04:50,960
Unit 1 wasn't under our control.

67
00:04:51,740 --> 00:04:52,880
This was an accident.

68
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:57,480
Thus, Unit 1 will remain frozen until the committee gives us further orders.

69
00:04:57,760 --> 00:04:58,280
Exactly.

70
00:04:58,980 --> 00:05:00,920
That is a very appropriate decision.

71
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:03,680
However, isn't your son still trapped inside it?

72
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:07,740
I knew this was hopeless.

73
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:09,640
It's not accepting the eject code.

74
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:11,160
What about the backup codes?

75
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:12,440
Also refused.

76
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:14,480
Even a direct circuit isn't getting through.

77
00:05:14,860 --> 00:05:16,860
But the plug's video monitor's still active.

78
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,500
I'm channeling it to the main screen.

79
00:05:20,540 --> 00:05:22,460
What in the hell is this?

80
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:25,880
This is the truth behind a 400% sync ratio.

81
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:27,560
I can't believe it.

82
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:29,140
What happened to Shinji?

83
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:31,300
He's been taken into Ava Unit 1.

84
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:32,780
Taken into it?

85
00:05:32,900 --> 00:05:34,300
What in the hell is an Ava?

86
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:37,200
It's a thing created by man in man's own image.

87
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:39,400
I really can't describe it any other way.

88
00:05:39,660 --> 00:05:40,840
Created by man?

89
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:42,680
You didn't create anything.

90
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:44,920
You just copied something you found in the Antarctic.

91
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:45,920
What was the original?

92
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:46,940
That's what I want to know.

93
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:48,740
This is not just a copy.

94
00:05:49,060 --> 00:05:50,760
A human will is inside it.

95
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:53,100
Are you saying somebody willed this to happen?

96
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:53,560
Yes.

97
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:54,360
The Ava did.

98
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:57,260
Do something, damn it!

99
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:58,760
You created this, didn't you?

100
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:01,080
Take responsibility for what you've done!

101
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:12,220
In regard to the issue of the Nansa Islands, the government and the Ministry of Internal Affairs have officially announced that there is no federal involvement.

102
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:17,280
It has been a month since the terrorist incident in Tokyo, too, and the government has...

103
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:18,380
I'm still alive.

104
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:23,060
I know that Wonder Girl's still alive!

105
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:26,220
Don't bother me with trivial crap like that, Misato!

106
00:06:28,220 --> 00:06:29,920
I can't believe it.

107
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:32,260
I couldn't do anything.

108
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:36,820
I can't believe that stupid Shinji outperformed me.

109
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:39,700
I can't stand it!

110
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:44,180
What do you mean you're going to salvage Shinji?

111
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:48,580
Well, theoretically, Shinji's life force still exists in there.

112
00:06:48,780 --> 00:06:49,020
Ha!

113
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:51,640
And will you be respecting that life this time?

114
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:54,800
Losing Shinji is out of the question now.

115
00:06:55,140 --> 00:06:56,060
Oh, I don't know.

116
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:59,200
What Nerve wants is Unit 1 as their tool, not Shinji.

117
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:00,600
I don't deny it.

118
00:07:00,780 --> 00:07:06,340
Our assumption is that Shinji's body lost its ego border, and that he's now floating in the entry plug in quantum form.

119
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:09,960
You're saying that Shinji has shifted into a form we can't see?

120
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:10,740
Yes.

121
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:15,720
The LCL has chemically altered into something very similar to the seawater of primitive Earth.

122
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:20,380
In fact, it's almost identical to the primordial soup we've duplicated in laboratories.

123
00:07:20,780 --> 00:07:21,700
Primordial soup?

124
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:22,320
Yes.

125
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:28,080
All of the substances which composed Shinji are still preserved in the plug, and his soul exists there as well.

126
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:32,140
In fact, his ego image is giving a sort of substance to his plug suit.

127
00:07:32,140 --> 00:07:37,200
In other words, this salvage operation must both reconstruct his body and return his soul into it.

128
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:38,360
Is that possible?

129
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:42,180
Possible? With the Magi's support? Yes, it is.

130
00:07:42,260 --> 00:07:44,760
This is all theoretical stuff you're talking about, isn't it?

131
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:47,320
You won't know what will really happen until you do it.

132
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:53,500
What is this?

133
00:07:54,660 --> 00:07:55,680
Where am I?

134
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:58,240
The entry plug of Unit 1?

135
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:00,720
But there's nobody here.

136
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:02,320
Not even myself.

137
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:04,500
What is this?

138
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:05,800
What is this?

139
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:07,220
What is this?

140
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:08,660
I don't understand.

141
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:10,600
These people.

142
00:08:11,820 --> 00:08:13,000
Yes, they're people I know.

143
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,320
People who know me.

144
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:17,520
I understand now.

145
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:19,100
This is my world.

146
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:20,940
What is this?

147
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:24,240
This is supposed to be my world, but this I don't understand.

148
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:25,840
An image from outside.

149
00:08:26,220 --> 00:08:27,080
A hostile image.

150
00:08:27,780 --> 00:08:28,480
That's right.

151
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:29,240
The enemy.

152
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:30,520
Enemy.

153
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:30,700
Enemy.

154
00:08:31,020 --> 00:08:31,300
Enemy.

155
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:31,400
Enemy.

156
